kusari/kusari
kusari/kusari.exe
.claude

# Built binaries and release artifacts.
#
# These are deliberately broad. Anything untracked and not ignored here is
# picked up by `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`, so it lands in the
# scan bundle -- and `git diff --binary` embeds an untracked binary in the patch
# as base85, which is what the analyzer reads. A ~30 MB executable becomes a
# ~37 MB blob and roughly 19 million tokens, well past any model's limit, and
# the scan fails with an error that says nothing about the real cause.
#
# The two lines at the top only cover binaries built inside kusari/. Building at
# the repo root (go build -o kusari.exe ./kusari) lands one here instead.
/kusari.exe
/kusari-cli
/kusari-cli.exe
*.exe

# goreleaser output; hundreds of MB across every target platform.
/dist/
